Work that runs on a schedule is a document in `{{ index .Caps "routine.schedule" }}/`,
not a cron entry somebody added once:

    ilk routine list                 what runs, and what is overdue for review
    ilk routine new "..."            write one
    ilk routine sync                 project them into what actually runs them

Reach for a routine last. A check, a hook or a gate that fires when somebody causes the
problem is better than a job that finds it at 4am, because it fires while the fix is
still cheap and the author still has the context.

Every routine carries a budget and an owner, and `ilk routine sync` must be run and
committed after any change to one — the schedule that runs is a projection, and `ilk
check` reports the two disagreeing.
